<title>USA: Catalina Marketing countersues Inter-Act.</title>
<headline>Catalina Marketing countersues Inter-Act.</headline>
<dateline>ST. PETERSBURG, Fla. 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Catalina Marketing Corp said Thursday it has filed a countersuit against Inter-Act Systems Inc, alleging patent infringement.</p>
<p>The suit involves a U.S. patent issued to Catalina on March 18, it said. The patent protects the company's method of issuing incentives and other communications based on consumer purchasing patterns, it said.</p>
<p>Neither a company spokesman nor its attorney were available to provide further details.</p>
<p>Catalina provides in-store electronic marketing programs for more than 150 companies.</p>
</text>
